A15. A revolver. ~ ROTOR
A16. This means to be certain. ~ SURE
A17. This bird talks like the Senator from Alabama. ~ PARROT
A19. This egg is a bad one. ~ ROTTEN
A21. To astonish. ~ STUN
A22. Part of a loud speaker. ~ LIP
A24. People rest easy when in this. ~ COMA
A26. Part of the verb to be. ~ AM
A27. These are wide open in tropical countries. ~ PORES
A29. Two famous sky-scrapers. ~ WE
A31. Charlie Paddock seems to enjoy running better than this man. ~ CAL
A33. This stays out all night on Broadway. ~ REVELER
A35. This is a hole-in-the-wall. ~ GAP
A37. This man is all wet—we hope. ~ AL
A38. This climbs around a lot. ~ VINE
A39. This has wooden limbs. ~ TREE
A41. A prefix signifying again. ~ RE
